DATA='Point potential|V=ke*q/r|V,q,r|ss+|Zero potential at infinity.|P:r,-ke*q;P:-ke,V*r;P:V,-ke*q\nCharge potential energy|U=ke*q1*q2/r|U,q1,q2,r|sss+|Signed pair energy; zero at infinity.|P:r,-ke*q1*q2;P:-ke*q2,U*r;P:-ke*q1,U*r;P:U,-ke*q1*q2\nPotential energy change|U=q*dV|U,q,dV|sss|U here means CHANGE in potential energy.|P:1,-dV*q;P:-dV,U;P:-q,U\nUniform field voltage|dV=-Ef*d|dV,Ef,d|sss|d along chosen field axis; uniform field.|P:1,Ef*d;P:d,dV;P:Ef,dV\nElectric work|W=-q*dV|W,q,dV|sss|Work done by electric force.|P:1,dV*q;P:dV,W;P:q,W\nRing axis potential|V=ke*Q/sqrt(x^2+R^2)|V,Q,x,R|sss+|Uniform ring; zero at infinity.|P:sqrt(R^2 + x^2),-Q*ke;P:-ke,V*sqrt(R^2 + x^2);E:-sqrt(Q^2*ke^2/V^2 - R^2),sqrt(Q^2*ke^2/V^2 - R^2);E:-sqrt(Q^2*ke^2/V^2 - x^2),sqrt(Q^2*ke^2/V^2 - x^2)\nSphere inside potential|V=ke*Q*(3-r^2/R^2)/(2*R)|V,Q,r,R|ss++|Uniform solid sphere; r<=R; V infinity=0.|P:2*R^3,-3*Q*R^2*ke + Q*ke*r^2;P:-3*R^2*ke + ke*r^2,2*R^3*V;P:Q*ke,0,-3*Q*R^2*ke + 2*R^3*V;E:\nShell inside potential|V=ke*Q/R|V,Q,R|ss+|Thin charged sphere/conductor; inside.|P:R,-Q*ke;P:-ke,R*V;P:V,-Q*ke\nLine potential diff|dV=-lam*ln(R/r)/(2*pi*eps0)|dV,lam,R,r|ss++|Infinite line; dV=V(R)-V(r).|P:2*pi*eps0,lam*ln(R/r);P:ln(R/r),2*pi*dV*eps0;E:r*exp(-2*pi*dV*eps0/lam);E:R*exp(2*pi*dV*eps0/lam)\nElectric kinetic energy|Kf-Ki=-q*dV|Kf,Ki,q,dV|00ss|Only electric force does work.|P:1,-Ki + dV*q;P:-1,Kf + dV*q;P:dV,Kf - Ki;P:q,Kf - Ki\nRod axis field|Ef=ke*lam*(1/x-1/(x+l))|Ef,lam,x,l|sss+|Uniform rod; target x>0 beyond near end.|P:l*x + x^2,-ke*l*lam;P:-ke*l,Ef*l*x + Ef*x^2;P:Ef,Ef*l,-ke*l*lam;P:Ef*x - ke*lam,Ef*x^2\nRod axis potential|V=ke*lam*ln((x+l)/x)|V,lam,x,l|sss+|Uniform rod; target x>0 beyond near end.|P:1,-ke*lam*ln(l/x + 1);P:-ke*ln(l/x + 1),V;E:l/(exp(V/(ke*lam)) - 1);E:x*(exp(V/(ke*lam)) - 1)'
